So, And in http://groups.yahoo.com/group/jboske/message/1732 says that 
Unique does work as an intensional:



I want A Doctor (A Doctor is the kind of thing I want)
I draw A Doctor (A Doctor is the kind of thing I draw)

And there is a Kind of 6-letter gismu, which you can talk about 
wanting, needing, describing, though it may end up having no denotation.



I could start pondering whether that works, but 
http://groups.yahoo.com/group/jboske/message/1736 (the Big Rethink) 
says no, intensional isn't a Unique, because you can intensionally want 
masses as well, and the Unique, whatever it is, is an individual. Right?



So we are indeed back to square one. You know, you'd get your 
cross-cutting with ka'ai too: leka'ai, leika'ai, le'ika'ai, lo malkampu 
be leika'ai... [Jordan, your football team takes it up the khyber]...



